n| **Trained by**  |  LLM-OS-Models⟨28⟩ · code at gyunggyung/long-gdn⟨49⟩  |  \n* * *\n##   ⟨45⟩ 1. Purpose \nVanilla GDN-2 370M baseline trained on the same 5B-token slice as `dsc-370m-fineweb-edu-5b-v3`, so the DSC vs vanilla comparison is apples-to-apples (same data, same compute, same hyperparameters).\n##   ⟨46⟩ 2. RULER results (vs DSC v3 5B) \nDSC v3 vs Vanilla 5B comparison is the **5B verdict** that determines whether DSC is a useful architectural addition to GDN-2. Full results in `docs/DSC_LIVE_STATUS_KO.md`. This vanilla checkpoint is the _floor_ that DSC improvement is measured against.\n##   ⟨47⟩ 3. Known limitations \n  * 5B tokens below Chinchilla optimal (~7.5B for 370M params)\n  * Long-context (≥16K) retrieval fails completely (vanilla linear attention state collapse) — the gap DSC is designed to close\n\n\n##   ⟨48⟩ 4. Citation \n\n```\n@misc{gdn2-vanilla-5b-2026,\n  author = {LLM-OS-Models},\n  title  = {GDN-2 370M FineWeb-Edu 5B vanilla baseline},\n  year   = {2026},\n  url    = {https://huggingface.co/LLM-OS-Models/gdn2-370m-fineweb-edu-5b}\n}\n\n```\nDownloads last month\n    \n-     \nDownloads are not tracked for this model. How to track ⟨50⟩\nInference Providers NEW⟨51⟩\n Text Generation ⟨52⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨53⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨54⟩ Privacy⟨55⟩ About⟨56⟩ Careers⟨57⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\nInference providers allow you to run inference using different serverless providers.\n",
